        ],
        "text": "According to Joseph L. Parkhurst (Petitioner), according to Joseph L. Parkhurst (Petitioner), the case concerns whether a pat\u2011down (frisk) of a vehicle passenger after a lawful traffic stop is permissible under the principles established in Pennsylvania v.\u202fMimms and related precedent."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "81f57b4e35a91ef51e80afc479a66b010b40d0622231c06211e8476d3366f7a0",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-81f57b4e35a9-0003-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 56,
              "start": 56
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kennedy, the Court is asked to decide whether Officer Trevizo had reasonable suspicion that the passenger, Johnson, was armed and dangerous at the time of the frisk."
      }
